From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 00:23:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] UefiPayloadPkg/CfrSetupMenuDxe: Give each category its
 own form

All CFR forms end up in a single HII form, one after the other under
subtitles. Make the setup menu work for a bootloader that groups its
options into categories:

- Each top-level CFR form, up to eight, gets a form of its own, titled
  with the CFR form name; the main form links to them. The formset has the
  EDKII_IFR_FRONT_PAGE_FORMS_GUID class GUID, so the front page lists the
  categories. Suppressed forms and those beyond eight stay in the main
  form as before.
- Nested forms are processed recursively: they become subtitles (cards)
  with their options, and their dependency and flags apply to all of them.
  Before, a nested form read its name at the wrong offset (relative to the
  parent HOB instead of to itself).
- Options get consecutive question IDs from CFR_COMPONENT_START. They were
  the low 16 bits of CFR_COMPONENT_START plus the 64-bit CFR object ID,
  which coreboot derives from pointers, so two options could collide.
- Boolean options are checkboxes instead of Enabled/Disabled lists, which
  graphical displays draw as switches. A checkbox uses the first byte of
  the 32-bit variable, which holds 0 or 1, and RouteConfig keeps the
  variable size, so existing variables and the bootloader are unaffected.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
